 CombineStatus←{
⍝ Takes the two indicators `git status --short` reports for a file - index and working area -
⍝ and returns a single one that describes the file in the working area compared with the last
⍝ commit, no matter whether a change is staged or not:
⍝ * "?" untracked
⍝ * "D" gone from the working area
⍝ * "A" unknown to the last commit
⍝ * "M" anything else, a rename included: the last commit knows that file under its old name
⍝ * " " a file that was added and deleted again: there is nothing to compare
     '??'≡⍵:'?'
     'AD'≡⍵:' '
     'D'∊⍵:'D'
     'A'=⊃⍵:'A'
     'M'
 }
